---
TDL: 0.2
Shell: 0.1
Name: List
---

# A scrolling list (Standard Modules > List): its entries are the call's children, usually a `For`
# keyed by an id. The wheel scrolls it (it is 240 by 200 pixels unless the call writes a `Width` or
# a `Height`). An entry has a key (a `For` entry the repeater's key, any other writes `Key: name`);
# a click chooses it: `Selection: SINGLE` (the default) takes the click, `NONE` ignores it.
# `Selected` is the chosen entry's key, set from outside (it marks the entry and raises nothing);
# `On_Changed` fires when the user chooses one (`event.old`, `event.new` and `event.value` are the
# keys). The chosen entry takes the style state `:selected` (and the role LISTITEM carries
# `selected`), so give the entries a class and style `.list_item:selected`; the Default stylesheet
# does for the class `list_item`. The role is LIST.
# Keys: the List is one Tab stop and its entries are reached with the arrow keys. Up and Down move
# the chosen entry (the first Down chooses the first entry, the first Up the last), Page Up and
# Page Down by a page, Home and End to the ends, Enter and Space choose the first entry when none
# is chosen, and letters typed jump to the next entry whose text starts with them (a space in a
# search is a letter of it; the search ends a second after the last letter). Each move is a choice:
# `On_Changed` fires and the entry scrolls into view. A disabled entry is passed over, a List with
# `Selection: NONE` takes no key, and a focused List keeps the keys, so they do not scroll a
# ScrollBox around it.
#   List { Selected: <| picked |>, On_Changed: choose, Children { For ... Key <| w.id |> { ... } } }
Module {
    Params {
        Selected { Type: string, Default: "" }
        Selection { Type: string, Default: SINGLE }
        Label { Type: string, Default: "" }
    }
    ScrollBox {
        Name: Root
        Role: LIST
        Label: <| params.Label |>
        Selection_Mode: <| params.Selection |>
        Chosen: <| params.Selected |>
        Width: 240
        Height: 200
        Children {
            FlexBox {
                Name: Items
                Flex: VERTICAL
                Align_Items: STRETCH
                Children { Content { } }
            }
        }
    }
}
